Social Network Friend Recommendation System Using C++

1. About Our Project

Our project recommends new friends to users based on mutual friends. We use C++ programming, Data Structures and Algorithms (DSA), and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) to manage users, friendships, and recommendations.

2. Team Members and Their Work

Samiksha – User Management: Manages user information.

Shivam – Graph and Friendship: Creates and manages friendship connections.

Rashi – Mutual Friends: Finds common friends between users.

Abhay – Recommendation System: Suggests potential new friends.

Ridham – Ranking and Sorting: Ranks recommendations based on mutual friends.

Anjali – Integration and Testing: Combines different modules and checks the overall working of the project.


3. Result

The system can store user information, represent friendships, identify mutual friends, and recommend potential friends based on common connections. The final results depend on the implemented and tested code.

4. Conclusion

Our project demonstrates how DSA and OOP concepts can be used to develop a simple friend recommendation system using C++. It improves our understanding of graphs, searching, sorting, and modular programming.
